1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,800
Here is the hot hydrogen
iodide tube again,

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:05,120
at about four hundred
and fifty degrees, where

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,560
K is forty-nine.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,960
But this time nobody let it settle first.

5
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:13,600
Someone has just mixed
0.20 moles per litre

6
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:18,400
of hydrogen, 0.20 of iodine and 0.50

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,840
of hydrogen iodide.

8
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,040
It has not reached
equilibrium, so something is

9
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,320
about to change.

10
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:27,120
Will the tube make more
hydrogen iodide, or

11
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:28,640
break some down?

12
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:30,720
There is a way to know before anything

13
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,440
moves.

14
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:35,386
So far K has always taken the settled

15
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:36,026
values.

16
00:00:36,587 --> 00:00:39,866
Now take the same fraction,
hydrogen iodide squared

17
00:00:39,947 --> 00:00:42,666
over hydrogen times iodine, and put in the

18
00:00:42,747 --> 00:00:45,706
concentrations in the tube
right now, settled or

19
00:00:45,787 --> 00:00:46,386
not.

20
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:49,466
That number is the reaction quotient, Q.

21
00:00:49,947 --> 00:00:52,026
It follows the same rules as K, with

22
00:00:52,107 --> 00:00:54,906
powers for coefficients,
and solids and the solvent

23
00:00:55,027 --> 00:00:55,546
left out.

24
00:00:56,107 --> 00:00:58,346
At equilibrium Q is K.

25
00:00:58,747 --> 00:01:01,146
At any other moment, Q can be any

26
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:01,786
value.

27
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,520
Substitute the values now.

28
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:09,720
Hydrogen iodide squared
is 0.50 squared, which is

29
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:11,560
0.25.

30
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:16,600
Underneath, hydrogen
times iodine is 0.20 times

31
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:21,080
0.20, which is 0.040.

32
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:26,200
So Q is 0.25 over 0.040,

33
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:28,280
which is 6.25.

34
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:30,940
Now compare it with K.

35
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:33,900
Each tick on this line is ten times

36
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,860
the one before, so small and large numbers

37
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:37,500
fit on it.

38
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:42,220
Q is 6.25 and K is forty-nine, so

39
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:44,340
Q is smaller than K.

40
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:47,340
Compared with the reactants,
this tube holds less

41
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,660
hydrogen iodide than
a settled tube at this

42
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:50,780
temperature would.

43
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:54,300
So which reaction is quicker,
hydrogen and iodine

44
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:57,500
joining, or hydrogen iodide splitting?

45
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:00,700
So which reaction wins?

46
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:03,820
Q compares products
with reactants, just like K

47
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:04,300
does.

48
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:07,820
Q is smaller than K, so compared with

49
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:10,460
a settled tube at this
temperature, this tube

50
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:13,740
holds too little hydrogen
iodide and too much

51
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:15,180
hydrogen and iodine.

52
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:18,780
With more hydrogen and iodine
to collide, joining

53
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:20,700
happens faster than splitting.

54
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:24,140
So the forward reaction
wins, and hydrogen iodide

55
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:24,940
is made.

56
00:02:26,167 --> 00:02:29,126
As hydrogen iodide forms, the top of Q

57
00:02:29,207 --> 00:02:32,806
grows and the bottom shrinks, so Q climbs.

58
00:02:33,047 --> 00:02:36,246
The forward rate falls,
the reverse rate rises,

59
00:02:36,327 --> 00:02:38,406
just as in the flask videos, until the

60
00:02:38,487 --> 00:02:39,366
two are equal.

61
00:02:39,767 --> 00:02:43,366
That happens exactly
when Q reaches K, here

62
00:02:43,527 --> 00:02:48,406
at 0.10, 0.10 and 0.70,

63
00:02:48,487 --> 00:02:51,286
the settled tube from the ICE table video,

64
00:02:51,367 --> 00:02:53,286
where Q is forty-nine.

65
00:02:53,367 --> 00:02:54,966
Q chases K.

66
00:02:56,167 --> 00:02:58,006
Now start from the other side.

67
00:02:58,247 --> 00:03:02,706
A tube holds 0.05 of hydrogen, 0.05 of

68
00:03:02,967 --> 00:03:07,406
iodine and 0.80 of hydrogen iodide.

69
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:10,886
That is almost all
hydrogen iodide, so does

70
00:03:11,047 --> 00:03:11,846
nothing more form?

71
00:03:12,247 --> 00:03:13,206
Work out Q.

72
00:03:13,847 --> 00:03:18,486
0.80 squared is 0.64, over 0.05

73
00:03:18,647 --> 00:03:24,806
times 0.05, which is 0.0025,

74
00:03:24,887 --> 00:03:27,606
so Q is 256.

75
00:03:27,767 --> 00:03:29,366
K is forty-nine.

76
00:03:29,447 --> 00:03:30,806
Which way will it run?

77
00:03:30,887 --> 00:03:32,166
Pause here to answer.

78
00:03:42,567 --> 00:03:45,446
Q is above K, so this tube has

79
00:03:45,527 --> 00:03:48,006
too much hydrogen iodide
for this temperature.

80
00:03:48,487 --> 00:03:51,366
Now splitting happens
faster than joining, so the

81
00:03:51,447 --> 00:03:52,966
reverse reaction wins.

82
00:03:53,447 --> 00:03:56,886
Hydrogen iodide splits,
Q falls, and the tube

83
00:03:56,967 --> 00:03:58,966
ends at the same settled tube again.

84
00:03:59,607 --> 00:04:02,166
The first tube had more
hydrogen iodide than

85
00:04:02,247 --> 00:04:08,326
hydrogen and iodine put
together, 0.50 against 0.40,

86
00:04:08,407 --> 00:04:10,726
yet its Q was below K.

87
00:04:11,047 --> 00:04:13,286
Whether there is too
much product depends on

88
00:04:13,367 --> 00:04:16,166
K, so work out Q and compare.

89
00:04:17,367 --> 00:04:19,846
If Q equals K, as in the settled

90
00:04:20,007 --> 00:04:22,566
tube, forward and reverse run at the same

91
00:04:22,647 --> 00:04:24,726
rate and nothing changes overall.

92
00:04:25,207 --> 00:04:28,726
That does not mean equal
concentrations: this tube

93
00:04:28,807 --> 00:04:34,166
has 0.10, 0.10 and 0.70.

94
00:04:34,207 --> 00:04:36,886
And if a flask holds only reactants, like

95
00:04:36,927 --> 00:04:38,406
the PCl₅ flask at the

96
00:04:38,487 --> 00:04:41,526
start, the top of Q is zero, so

97
00:04:41,687 --> 00:04:44,006
Q is below any K and the reaction

98
00:04:44,087 --> 00:04:44,886
runs forward.

99
00:04:45,447 --> 00:04:47,766
If it holds only products, the bottom is

100
00:04:47,847 --> 00:04:50,646
zero, Q is off the scale, above any

101
00:04:50,727 --> 00:04:52,806
K, and it runs in reverse.

102
00:04:54,034 --> 00:04:56,873
This also explains the disturbance videos.

103
00:04:57,154 --> 00:05:02,113
Take the settled tube, 0.10, 0.10 and

104
00:05:02,194 --> 00:05:06,113
0.70, where Q is forty-nine.

105
00:05:06,234 --> 00:05:08,993
Now, in the same sealed tube, add 0.20

106
00:05:09,154 --> 00:05:12,993
moles per litre of hydrogen,
so hydrogen is

107
00:05:13,114 --> 00:05:14,913
0.30.

108
00:05:14,994 --> 00:05:17,393
The bottom of Q gets bigger, so Q

109
00:05:17,554 --> 00:05:22,753
drops to 0.49 over 0.030, about sixteen,

110
00:05:22,834 --> 00:05:24,353
below K.

111
00:05:24,434 --> 00:05:26,513
Now there is too little product for this

112
00:05:26,754 --> 00:05:30,113
temperature, so the forward
reaction wins, uses up

113
00:05:30,194 --> 00:05:32,353
some of the extra hydrogen,
and the mixture

114
00:05:32,514 --> 00:05:33,393
shifts right.

115
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:37,560
Taking out some hydrogen
iodide does the same,

116
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:41,000
and adding hydrogen
iodide pushes Q above K

117
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:42,520
and sends it left.

118
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:46,040
K never changed: it is still forty-nine.

119
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:49,880
Adding or removing
a substance changes Q only.

120
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:52,680
Only a change of temperature
changes K, and

121
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:54,200
that is a later video.

122
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:56,320
Your turn.

123
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:59,640
Ammonia is made from
nitrogen and hydrogen in

124
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:02,440
a sealed vessel with
an iron catalyst, held

125
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:05,720
at four hundred degrees
Celsius, where K is

126
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:08,480
0.50 for this equation.

127
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,920
A mixture has just been made up, with

128
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,160
nitrogen at 0.40 moles
per litre, hydrogen at

129
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:19,880
0.50 and ammonia at 0.20.

130
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:23,240
One: calculate Q for N₂ plus three

131
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:26,600
H₂ making two NH₃.

132
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:29,400
Two: will the mixture make more ammonia or

133
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:31,120
less, and why?

134
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,680
Pause here to answer.

135
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:46,860
Write Q as ammonia squared
over nitrogen times

136
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,060
hydrogen cubed.

137
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:52,300
Ammonia squared is 0.040.

138
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:57,420
Hydrogen cubed is 0.50 times 0.50 times

139
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:02,300
0.50, 0.125, and times the nitrogen

140
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:05,340
that is 0.050.

141
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:11,100
So Q is 0.040 over 0.050,

142
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:13,500
which is 0.80.

143
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:17,420
Q is above K, 0.50, so the mixture

144
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:20,300
holds too much ammonia
for this temperature.

145
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:23,340
The reverse reaction
is faster and ammonia breaks

146
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:25,580
down, so it makes less.

147
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:28,620
If you got 0.20, you left the cube

148
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:31,100
off the hydrogen,
and that wrong number sits

149
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:33,500
below K, so you would have said more

150
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:34,620
ammonia.

151
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:37,660
If you found 0.80 and still said more

152
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:40,780
ammonia, you flipped the rule: a Q above

153
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:43,900
K means too much product, not too little.

154
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:46,860
So when a question gives you a mixture

155
00:07:46,940 --> 00:07:49,580
and a K, write the expression, put in

156
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:53,260
the concentrations from now,
calculate Q, and compare

157
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:55,260
it with K at the same temperature.

158
00:07:55,820 --> 00:07:58,380
Q below K, the reaction runs forward.

159
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,860
Q above K, it runs back.

160
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:03,500
Equal, nothing changes overall.

161
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:06,300
That gives you the direction, not how far

162
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:06,940
it goes.

163
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:10,380
Finding how far uses an ICE table and

164
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:13,180
K, and the harder cases come next.

165
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:15,840
Here are the key notes.

